# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 10 (a `~T` is a `T` or an `Error`; a bare `Error(..)` where a `~T` is wanted is that `~T`'s failure, and `r == Error(..)` is a plain test): each `Error` inside a value shows its message where the value meets its `~Nat`.
test error_inside

